      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "When using a self-built compiler on an Apple Silicon host to build a `x86_64-unknown-none` static library, `mach-o-arm64` objects get mixed into the output. This happens since https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/103732.\r\n\r\n# Problem setup\r\n\r\n```toml\r\n# config.toml\r\n# using stage1, built with `./x.py build`\r\nchangelog-seen = 2\r\n\r\n[llvm]\r\ntargets = \"AArch64;X86\"\r\n\r\n[build]\r\ntarget = [\r\n    \"aarch64-apple-darwin\",\r\n    \"x86_64-unknown-none\",\r\n]\r\n\r\n[rust]\r\nllvm-tools = true\r\nlld = true\r\n```\r\n\r\n```\r\nhost: aarch64-apple-darwin\r\n```\r\n\r\n```rust\r\n// foo.rs\r\n#![no_std]\r\n\r\n#[panic_handler]\r\nfn panic(_: &core::panic::PanicInfo) -> ! {\r\n    loop {}\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ rustc --crate-type staticlib --target x86_64-unknown-none foo.rs\r\n$ objdump --archive-headers libfoo.a\r\n```\r\n\r\n# Results\r\n\r\n1. 33b530e04099465a8029ef581202d52f4075558e\r\n    * [33b530e.log](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/files/10116319/33b530e.log)\r\n    * does not contain any `mach-o-arm64` files\r\n2. 5984b1d86f0e7221c83c0d63b8d63fc0de9c5760 (the next commit)\r\n    * [5984b1d.log](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/files/10116320/5984b1d.log)\r\n    * contains `absvdi2.o: file format mach-o-arm64` and more\r\n3. `nightly-2022-11-01` (the next nightly)\r\n    * [nightly-2022-11-01.log](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/files/10116427/nightly-2022-11-01.log)\r\n    * does not contain any `mach-o-arm64` files\r\n\r\nCC: @stlankes",
      "closed_at": "2026-01-05T22:04:36Z",
